<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stefan the First-Crowned</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1165–<a href="/years/1228">1228</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Stefan Nemanjić</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stefan the First-Crowned was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-nemanja">Stefan Nemanja</a> and ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from 1196 to 1228. He was crowned king in 1217 with a crown sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a>, raising Serbia to a kingdom, while his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-sava">Saint Sava</a> won an autocephalous Serbian church in 1219. His daughter Komnena married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhimiter-progoni">Dhimitër Progoni</a> of Arbanon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stefan-the-first-crowned.jpg" alt="Stefan the First-Crowned" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Afresco_Stefan_nemanjic_restored.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
